cff-version: 1.2.0
title: agentic-paper2code
message: >-
  If you use this toolkit, please cite both this repository and the Paper2Code
  paper it is built on, listed under references.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Hasan Taha
    family-names: Bagci
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-09-09'
url: https://github.com/hasantahabagci/agentic-paper2code
repository-code: https://github.com/hasantahabagci/agentic-paper2code
abstract: >-
  A ten-stage pipeline that reproduces a research paper as a working code
  repository, written as Markdown stage prompts executed by a coding agent
  rather than as an API-driven program. It adapts the planning, analysis and
  coding decomposition of Paper2Code and adds ingestion, configuration
  provenance, frozen interfaces, execution-based verification, fidelity review
  and packaging.
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - research-software
  - paper-implementation
  - coding-agents
license: Apache-2.0
references:
  - type: conference-paper
    title: >-
      Paper2Code: Automating Code Generation from Scientific Papers in
      Machine Learning
    authors:
      - given-names: Minju
        family-names: Seo
      - given-names: Jinheon
        family-names: Baek
      - given-names: Seongyun
        family-names: Lee
      - given-names: Sung Ju
        family-names: Hwang
    collection-title: International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR)
    year: 2026
    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.17192
